11","position":"1785010867902851001-78a4a457-e5a7-4fe1-aa38-c3e65dfd1627"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"688749aac8e54a36434c19e55c123f63b96ea39d7292918ff1f2ae61b18aa050","event_uuid":"5719da92-75be-4041-8444-faba6dd82042","position":{"commit_sha":"22cb51ec641fdf3ae12d81ce6482db5dd31e79c5","position":"1785011092949259458-5719da92-75be-4041-8444-faba6dd82042"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"5aca7285a13f5dc553cc0a2376d5e85aab59018e9fa0e79341bcf3009a6c807a","event_uuid":"6d5f334e-4325-4caa-8736-306916a32c79","position":{"commit_sha":"da10fe838d6b022bcb44bdc64607f33fe3cbf48e","position":"1785013068218945001-6d5f334e-4325-4caa-8736-306916a32c79"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"TDD contract card: authoritative_contract=signed 41e2 plan plus landed 8153 gate-aware calibrate seam; trigger_preconditions=synthetic repo activates project.foo in code_review only or in both plan_review+code_review; production_path=_criteria argparse -> _criteria_eval dual registry admission -> calibrate_criterion; test_tier=in-process CLI-handler unit because parser, repo resolution, registry lookups, exit codes, stdout/stderr, and dispatch all run real while calibration is the irreducible stub; observable_postconditions=one-gate calls calibrate once with repo root/runs, unknown and ambiguous return 1 with distinct diagnostics, help contains exact project.foo code-review example; ci_gate=pytest tests/unit/test_code_review_project_criteria.py -k cli; negative_control=unknown retains existing behavior; collateral/recovery/fault_injection=N/A. Collection: 4 selected/24 deselected. RED: 3 intended failures and 1 passing unknown control.","timestamp":1785010722973843001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Held-out TDD GREEN: standard-tier gpt-5.6-terra implementer succeeded in 1 attempt against the single visible one-gate CLI happy path. Restored unknown, both-gates ambiguity, and help cases: full selector 4/4 GREEN. Exact-defect mutation changed the dual-membership predicate so ambiguous project.foo reached calibration; the hidden ambiguity test went RED, then restoration returned 4/4 GREEN. Refactoring litmus passes: tests assert CLI exit codes, stdout/stderr, parser help, and calibration calls, not source layout or local variable names.","timestamp":1785010867902851001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Five-axis review and final local preflight GREEN: behavior matches exact-one-gate admission, distinct unknown and ambiguity diagnostics, and project.foo help contract; tests assert public parser/registry/dispatch observables and stub only live calibration; no new state mutation, security boundary, or material performance risk. Focused project-criteria suite 28 passed; Ruff and git diff checks passed; production module 311 LOC. Canonical gates: make lint PASS, make typecheck PASS (379 source files), make test PASS with 7213 passed / 29 skipped / 114 deselected / 13 known warnings in 1837.16s.","timestamp":1785013068218945001}],"created_at":1784670019530062001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"28a607a2-f78c-45d6-9132-1af692e58ea5","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"8153-e9b5-5706-49c8"},{"link_uuid":"1b05c89e-04d9-4e35-8faf-9871f8eb1f07","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"fc72-bf7e-7652-4228"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe `criteria eval` CLI admits only plan-review ids: its preflight rejects anything not in `plan_review.registry.by_id(repo_root)` (`src/rebar/_cli/_llm_eval_commands.py:143-155`), so an activated project **code-review** criterion is refused as \"unknown\" before the gate-aware eval resolver is ever reached. Fifth of five seams (root cause on superseded bug 8a4b).\n\n## Approach\n\nExtend the preflight to admit code-review ids and to resolve the target gate deterministically:\n\n- Look the id up in BOTH the plan-review effective registry and the code-review effective registry (`code_review.registry.effective_criteria(repo_root)`, `src/rebar/llm/code_review/registry.py:179-184`).\n- Admit iff present in **exactly one** gate; dispatch to the gate-aware calibrate path that child 4 `[rebar:8153-e9b5-5706-49c8]` adds to `calibrate_criterion`.\n- If the id is active in **both** gates, reject as **ambiguous** with a message telling the author which gates claim it; if in neither, keep the existing \"unknown\" error.\n- Update the subparser help text to include the concrete project code-review example `project.foo` alongside the plan-review example.\n\n**Rejected alternative.** Adding a `criteria eval --gate` flag — heavier UX for a rare case; the \"active in exactly one gate ⇒ resolve there\" rule covers the common path and only genuine cross-gate ambiguity needs operator input.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_llm_eval_commands.py` — dual-registry admission, one-gate resolution, ambiguity rejection, help text.\n- `tests/unit/test_code_review_project_criteria.py` — append CLI cases to this shared test file, which was created by child 1 `[rebar:fc72-bf7e-7652-4228]`. This ticket depends on child 1 and child 4 `[rebar:8153-e9b5-5706-49c8]`; tests build a synthetic repo activating `project.foo` as a code-review criterion.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Happy path (CLI): `project.foo`, active in code-review only, is admitted and reaches the calibrate call with exit 0.\n- Unknown edge: an id active in neither registry returns exit 1 and emits the existing \"unknown\" message.\n- Ambiguity edge: `project.foo` active in both registries returns exit 1 and emits an \"ambiguous\" message naming `plan_review` and `code_review`.\n- Help text: `criteria eval --help` contains the exact substring `project.foo` in the code-review example.\n\nTier: unit — invoke the command handler with a synthetic-repo `repo_root`, with calibration stubbed.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A one-gate project code-review id is admitted and dispatched to the code-review calibrate path; verified by `rtk .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_code_review_project_criteria.py -k cli`.\n- [ ] An unknown id is rejected with exit 1 and the existing distinct \"unknown\" message; verified by the same `-k cli` selector.\n- [ ] An id active in both gates is rejected with exit 1 and an \"ambiguous\" message naming `plan_review` and `code_review`; verified by the same `-k cli` selector.\n- [ ] `criteria eval --help` contains the exact code-review example substring `project.foo`; verified by the same `-k cli` selector.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_llm_eval_commands.py","reason":"Dual-registry admission, one-gate resolution, ambiguity rejection, help text"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_code_review_project_criteria.py","reason":"CLI admit/reject/ambiguous tests"}],"keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on","8153-e9b5-5706-49c8"],["depends_on","fc72-bf7e-7652-4228"],["parent","119f-63e3-34b7-4f96"]],"parent_id":"119f-63e3-34b7-4f96","parent_status_uuid":"e3325ba6-1f8e-4f98-b476-b3928312c006","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["review-architecture","project-criteria","integration"],"ticket_id":"41e2-a0a2-2db4-4847","ticket_type":"story","title":"Admit one-gate project code-review ids in the criteria eval CLI","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["8fa24068-c29c-4ec2-8581-f27b3b8a013c","d34a74ec-e8cf-4d26-84ed-d7db3544c9f3","acf0da03-d03a-4820-926d-da3622b8c5ca","28a607a2-f78c-45d6-9132-1af692e58ea5","59917465-8c73-4e77-8612-838f3aa206a4","e86ddead-4e05-401b-a6a8-539987851a29","1b05c89e-04d9-4e35-8faf-9871f8eb1f07","c15dc0ea-61ed-451f-bc5c-acac8d0c95a1","96989c73-e2ef-4c68-872a-41ffebc6ebc2","d28a70ec-89cc-413d-979a-ae7b22990b97","1fb65374-ba44-498a-9cc3-c2fd984f652c","e3325ba6-1f8e-4f98-b476-b3928312c006","7850041c-f98f-481c-ae84-63cd88dec4b4","aaa14800-8163-492d-bcf8-7f36a3f24149","78a4a457-e5a7-4fe1-aa38-c3e65dfd1627","5719da92-75be-4041-8444-faba6dd82042","6d5f334e-4325-4caa-8736-306916a32c79"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785013068218945002,"uuid":"aa017f2c-3b25-41e1-86cc-bb17b266c56f"}